                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose the gap, not the request`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `Summit's RFP says “leadership training,” but its own engagement survey describes <strong>unclear decision rights and weak cross-functional coordination</strong> — managers who can't translate a grid-modernisation strategy into operational change. The presenting request and the real capability gap are not the same thing. Separate them, decide how much of this an education programme can actually move versus what only org design can fix, and commit to a Level 3–4 success measure you can defend in six months. The trap: <em>designing to the request, not the gap</em>, and promising impact you can't audit.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Architect the blueprint`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Turn the diagnosis into a design for 220 managers. Choose the <strong>format mix</strong> — in-person maximises transfer but blows the ceiling, all-virtual scales cheaply but transfers shallowly, blended-with-digital balances both. Then pick the <strong>transfer mechanism</strong> that actually earns your Level 3 promise, decide cohort waves across the 90-day window, and size the journey. The trap: <em>format by default</em> and an impact promise with no transfer — and a beautiful 9-module blueprint that can't be signed in 18 days.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Allocate faculty & cost the margin`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Staff the energy-transition modules with only <strong>2 internal academics</strong> (both committed through Q2) and an external bench at <strong>1.5× day-rates</strong>, then build the engagement P&L against the <strong>$1.8M ceiling</strong>. Pick a margin-protection lever that protects the diagnosis, size the design/platform investment, and make the bid call: full-custom loss-leader, scaled-custom that holds the 22% floor, or a disciplined no-bid. The trap: <em>margin blindness</em> — pricing to win while the contribution margin silently falls below the floor.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Pitch, defend & de-risk`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Pitch the COO and CHRO and survive the probe: “How do you know this moves operational performance, not just confidence?” Walk the evidence chain from diagnosed gap to the named operational KPI, name the single biggest delivery risk and its mitigation, and state the renewal logic toward the 3-year, <strong>~$6M master agreement</strong>. The trap: <em>retreating to confidence-and-engagement</em> when pressed, denying any risk, and never connecting this engagement to the preferred-provider prize.`,

                    r1_gap_label:           `Summit says “leadership training.” What is the real capability gap the data shows?`,
                    gap_coordination:       `Unclear decision rights & weak cross-functional coordination translating strategy into operational change`,
                    gap_leadership:         `A generic leadership-skills gap — exactly what the client asked for`,
                    gap_technical:          `A technical knowledge gap — managers don't understand grid-modernisation tech`,
                    gap_motivation:         `A motivation gap — the managers just need to be inspired and energised`,
                    r1_root_label:          `Map the dominant root cause. Which part is genuinely an education problem?`,
                    root_mixed:             `Mixed — education moves the skill/decision-confidence part; flag the org-design part for the client`,
                    root_alleducation:      `It's all an education problem — a programme fixes everything Summit raised`,
                    root_allorgdesign:      `It's all org design — decline; there is nothing education can do here`,
                    r1_measure_label:       `Which Level 3–4 success measures will you commit to in the impact dossier?`,
                    meas_behaviorkpi:       `On-the-job behaviour change + a named operational KPI (cycle-time, outage response) at 6–12 months`,
                    meas_reaction:          `Level 1–2 only — satisfaction scores and an end-of-course knowledge test`,
                    meas_vague:             `A vague promise of “improved leadership capability” with no defined metric`,
                    r1_rigor_label:         `How rigorously does your team interrogate the survey evidence before designing? (%)`,
                    r1_rigor_readout:       `Diagnostic rigour applied to the evidence:`,

                    r2_format_label:        `Choose the format mix for 220 managers — weigh transfer-of-learning AND the ceiling`,
                    format_blended:         `Blended-with-digital — live-virtual core, targeted in-person intensives, digital pre-work`,
                    format_inperson:        `All in-person — five campus days for all 220 to maximise engagement`,
                    format_virtual:         `All live-virtual — cheapest, scales easily across the operations footprint`,
                    r2_transfer_label:      `Transfer mechanism — what forces learning to reach Level 3 on the job?`,
                    transfer_projectcoach:  `Live application projects on the real grid transition + manager coaching + spaced reinforcement`,
                    transfer_assignment:    `A reflective post-course assignment graded by faculty`,
                    transfer_none:          `None — the workshop content is strong enough; transfer will happen naturally`,
                    r2_cohort_label:        `Cohort structure across the 90-day window`,
                    cohort_staggered:       `Staggered waves — pilot one cohort, learn, refine, then spread to the rest`,
                    cohort_onewave:         `One wave — all 220 at once to hit the deadline fastest`,
                    r2_modules_label:       `How many modules in the blueprint? (deeper ≠ better if it can't be built in 18 days)`,
                    r2_modules_hint:        `A focused 5–6 module journey is signable in 18 days; a 9+ module co-design is not.`,

                    r3_faculty_label:       `Staff the energy-transition modules. Only 2 internal academics, both committed through Q2.`,
                    faculty_blend:          `Anchor with the 2 internal academics for brand-critical modules; fill gaps with the vetted external bench`,
                    faculty_external:       `All external bench — fastest to staff, even at 1.5× day-rates`,
                    faculty_forceinternal:  `Force both internal academics off their Q2 commitments to teach everything`,
                    r3_lever_label:         `Pick ONE margin-protection lever that does NOT break the diagnosis`,
                    lever_reuse:            `Reuse validated content assets & shift volume to the cheaper-transfer live-virtual core`,
                    lever_cutdays:          `Cut the application projects and manager coaching to save cost`,
                    lever_cutpax:           `Drop coverage to 120 managers and bill the same — leave 100 untrained`,
                    r3_design_label:        `Design & platform investment (materials, LMS, digital build) — $k`,
                    r3_design_hint:         `$k for design hours, platform and materials. Under-investing starves transfer; over-investing erases the margin.`,
                    r3_bid_label:           `The bid decision under the $1.8M ceiling`,
                    bid_full:               `Full-custom at $1.8M as a deliberate, defensible loss-leader for the 3-year master agreement`,
                    bid_scaled:             `Scaled-custom — same diagnosis, leaner delivery, margin held at or above the 22% floor`,
                    bid_nobid:              `No-bid — the gap, timeline and margin can't all be met; protect the brand`,
                    bid_pricetowin:         `Price to win at any cost — all-external bench, ignore the margin, just take the bake-off`,

                    r4_defend_label:        `The COO presses: “How do you know this moves operational performance, not just confidence?”`,
                    defend_evidence:        `Walk the chain: diagnosed gap → transfer design → leading behaviour indicators → the named operational KPI in the dossier`,
                    defend_trust:           `Point to Wasatch's reputation and past satisfaction scores`,
                    defend_reframe:         `Reframe — promise confidence and engagement gains instead of measured business impact`,
